    <summary>PST password remover for Outlook data files you own: recovers a working password or clears it in seconds, for single archives or batches, with everything kept on your PC.</summary>
    <description>Outlook PST Password Remover and Recovery Software is a commercial Windows utility, and in short a PST password remover for Outlook data files that you own. It reads a .pst archive, finds a password that matches the stored one and can also clear the protection. For anyone who looks after several PCs it is a self-contained package, since it brings no GPU driver, word list or extra tool with it.

![Outlook PST Password Recovery screenshot 1](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/opr/opr-v4-list.png)

## Before you install

This package installs the free trial of a commercial program. A paid license unlocks what the trial withholds, and the Trial and license section below lists it.

## How to use this PST password remover

1. Start the program and add .pst files to the list.
2. Press Start. The program answers in about a second for each archive.
3. Read the result window with the recovered password and the file name.
4. Save the unlocked copy, or type the password into Outlook.

Trial note: the free trial performs the whole run and displays the result, but it shows only the first letter of the password and does not save an unlocked .pst. A license removes both limits.

![Outlook PST Password Recovery screenshot 2](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/opr/opr-v4-run.png)

## Who needs to remove password from PST file archives

- People who need to remove password from PST file archives they protected long ago and then lost the password to.
- Help desk staff who get a PST file from a user and need to unlock it without sending it away.
- Administrators who want a PST password remover that runs offline on a workstation.

## Why it is fast

A .pst password is a 32-bit checksum kept in the file, not a lock on the data. The program computes a string with the same checksum, so no dictionary, mask or graphics card is needed to remove password from PST file archives. Native .pst files of both the ANSI and Unicode kind are supported. The recovered password can differ from the original because of a checksum collision, but it opens the archive. Offline storage files with the .ost extension have no such password and are out of scope.

![Outlook PST Password Recovery screenshot 3](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/opr/opr-v4-saved.png)

## Trial and license

The trial installed by this package never alters your archive. Seeing the full password and saving a copy without protection requires a license from SoftOrbits, available as a lifetime license, a one-year license or a business license for several PCs. See [Outlook PST Password Recovery](https://www.softorbits.net/outlook-pst-password-recovery/?utm_source=chocolatey&amp;utm_medium=package) for plans.

## FAQ

### How do I recover my password for email on Outlook if I forgot my password?

This program covers the password on a .pst data file, which is separate from the sign-in of a mail account. For an archive, run the file through it and use the password it returns.

### How can I find my Outlook PST password without resetting it?

You can read it back from the file itself. The program recovers a password with the same checksum as the stored one, so the archive needs no reset and stays unchanged.

### What should a password recovery tool for Outlook PST files do?

It should work locally, accept several archives and handle both ANSI and Unicode files. It should also say plainly what it cannot touch, which here means .ost files.
